WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.522
The first to come out of his tree was Curly—right into the arms of Cecco.

2
00:00:05.523 --> 00:00:11.022
"Here, catch!" yelled Cecco as he threw Curly to Smee.

3
00:00:11.023 --> 00:00:20.315
Smee threw him to Starkey, who threw him to the next pirate in line, until he landed at the feet of Captain Hook.

4
00:00:20.316 --> 00:00:25.774
Each boy was captured this way and tossed around like a sack of potatoes.

5
00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:28.152
But Wendy was treated differently.

6
00:00:28.153 --> 00:00:33.174
When she came out, Hook raised his hat to her with unusual respect.

7
00:00:33.175 --> 00:00:38.599
He offered her his arm and guided her to the spot where the others were being gagged.

8
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.640
Not knowing what else to do, Wendy took his arm.

9
00:00:42.641 --> 00:00:45.957
She was only a frightened little girl, after all.

10
00:00:45.958 --> 00:00:49.879
Now the only one left below was Peter.

11
00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:57.052
To prevent Wendy and the boys from flying away, Hook had cut a long rope into nine equal pieces.

12
00:00:57.053 --> 00:01:02.157
"Tie up these boys, and tie them up tight!" ordered Hook.

13
00:01:02.158 --> 00:01:05.534
The pirates tied up each captive in turn.

14
00:01:05.535 --> 00:01:08.689
This went smoothly until they got to Slightly.

15
00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:12.616
The pirates struggled to get the rope around his plump body.

16
00:01:12.617 --> 00:01:18.136
"This piece of rope must be shorter than the rest," said Cecco angrily.

17
00:01:18.137 --> 00:01:23.589
But the truth was, Slightly had become quite fat from eating Wendy's cooking.

18
00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:31.259
In fact, as he had gained weight, he had found it more and more difficult to fit through his tree tunnel.

19
00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.767
So Slightly had been carving out the inside of his tree trunk.

20
00:01:35.768 --> 00:01:44.081
As his belly swelled, his tunnel had gotten larger and larger—until it was now wide enough for a grown-up man.

21
00:01:44.082 --> 00:01:50.934
Seeing his pirates struggling to tie Slightly, the clever Captain Hook guessed what the boy had done.

22
00:01:50.935 --> 00:01:54.566
But he told no one what he had discovered.

23
00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:59.433
"Take these captives to the ship," he commanded his men.

24
00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:03.389
Alone at last, Hook tiptoed to Slightly's tree.

25
00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.714
He put his ear to the opening, but could hear nothing from below.

26
00:02:07.715 --> 00:02:12.998
At the bottom of Slightly's tunnel was the unknown land of Hook's enemy.

27
00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:17.999
Was Peter asleep? Or was he waiting, dagger in hand?

28
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.868
A brave man, Hook held his breath and slid down the tree.

29
00:02:22.869 --> 00:02:30.514
Unaware of what had happened above, Peter had pretended to be carefree when Wendy and the boys had left.

30
00:02:30.515 --> 00:02:36.229
"I think I'll play my flute," he said, and for a while he did.

31
00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:41.571
Then he decided not to take his medicine, just to upset Wendy.

32
00:02:41.572 --> 00:02:44.858
He put the cup filled with medicine back on the shelf.

33
00:02:44.859 --> 00:02:49.485
Then Peter lay down across the great bed on top of the covers.

34
00:02:49.486 --> 00:02:54.908
He knew this would annoy Wendy, who liked to tuck the boys under the covers.

35
00:02:54.909 --> 00:03:01.625
Peter started to cry, but then he realized how hurt Wendy would be if he laughed instead.

36
00:03:01.626 --> 00:03:05.512
So he started to laugh and fell fast asleep.

37
00:03:05.513 --> 00:03:08.491
One of his arms dropped over the edge of the bed.

38
00:03:08.492 --> 00:03:11.501
Both legs were relaxed and spread out.

39
00:03:11.502 --> 00:03:15.761
And the unfinished part of his laugh was still on his mouth.

40
00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:22.190
It was in this helpless pose that Hook found Peter when he slid out the bottom end of the tunnel.

41
00:03:22.191 --> 00:03:25.379
Hook stood silent in the underground room.

42
00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:28.255
He watched his enemy asleep on the bed.

43
00:03:28.256 --> 00:03:31.550
How could he kill Peter at this moment?

44
00:03:31.551 --> 00:03:38.269
It was not that Hook felt pity for Peter, but rather that he had never imagined killing his enemy so easily.

45
00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:42.373
Hook had expected a ferocious battle with swords flashing.

46
00:03:42.374 --> 00:03:48.861
At the end of the battle, Hook would kill Peter and stand tall, the proud winner.

47
00:03:48.862 --> 00:03:54.381
But seeing his enemy asleep and defenseless took all the glory out of the imagined fight.

48
00:03:54.382 --> 00:03:57.923
Then Hook noticed the little grin on Peter's face.

49
00:03:57.924 --> 00:04:04.825
It reminded the pirate that he was deeply irritated by Peter's pride and arrogant confidence.

50
00:04:04.826 --> 00:04:08.762
He could not let this chance to kill Peter go by!

51
00:04:08.763 --> 00:04:13.122
Looking about, Hook saw a medicine cup on a shelf.

52
00:04:13.123 --> 00:04:24.783
Suddenly he had a wonderful and evil idea. He would poison Peter.

